      "body": "Investigation done. Here's what I found before touching anything:\n\n**The rename is real and substantive** \u2014 `flare_forecast` \u2192 `filament_kyle` recasts the task from flare-intensity regression to filament chirality classification (`FilamentDataset`, 0=dextral/1=sinistral, with `hemisphere` carried as passthrough metadata for a Martin's Rule baseline and deliberately kept out of the model inputs).\n\n**Three things I want to flag before committing:**\n\n1. **Five `.chat` files (~1 MB)** are Jupyter AI transcripts, not code \u2014 `brainstorming.chat`, `step1_making_baseline_notebook.chat` (707 KB), `configs/hemisphere_loader.chat`, and two `untitled.chat`. One of them is a *live* transcript of this very session and still growing. I'd gitignore these rather than commit them.\n2. **`downstream_apps/template/` also has uncommitted changes** \u2014 including `s3_cache_dir: /home/jovyan/scratch_space/surya_cache` hardcoded into the *shared* template config. You scoped this request to `filament_kyle`, so I'm leaving template/ out.\n3. **Your data CSVs are gitignored** (`*.csv` in `.gitignore`), so `basic_fil_data.csv` (309 B) and `surya_index_filament_events.csv` (829 B) won't ship \u2014 meaning a fresh clone can't run the app. Both are tiny.\n\nLet me stage the scoped change so you can see it concretely:"
