            "raw_input": {
              "description": "Commit the scoped rename and changes",
              "command": "cd /home/jovyan/surya_workshop && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git log --stat --oneline -1 | head -30\nRecast flare_forecast app as filament chirality classification\n\nRenames downstream_apps/flare_forecast to downstream_apps/filament_kyle\nand retargets the task from flare-intensity regression to filament\nchirality classification against a 45-filament catalog.\n\n- FlareDSDataset -> FilamentDataset: the label is now chirality\n  (0 = dextral, 1 = sinistral), validated to be strictly 0/1 at init\n  rather than passed through a label_transform.\n- hemisphere is carried as passthrough metadata only. It drives the\n  Martin's Rule baseline and per-hemisphere accuracy reporting, and is\n  deliberately never fed to the model as an input feature, since that\n  would hand it the answer the Surya-vs-baseline comparison is meant\n  to test for.\n- FlareDataConfig -> FilamentDataConfig, load_flare_config ->\n  load_filament_config, flare_index_path replaces the old flare index\n  field, and ds_time_tolerance tightens from 4d to 2d.\n- Adds 1_baseline_filament.ipynb for the Martin's Rule baseline.\n- Ignores *.chat, the Jupyter AI transcript files the workflow leaves\n  scattered through the app directory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF"
            },
